  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Urban Health Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  USAID&apos;s Urban Health Activity is a new activity designed to address Bangladesh&apos;s systemic urban health issues. The activity will work with municipalities and city corporations to establish and strengthen urban health systems capable of providing quality and equitable health services to improve health outcomes among all urbanites. Using FY 2024 funds, this activity will support cities and municipalities to improve their capacity to plan, budget, and manage health systems, strengthening urban health systems overall and contributing to the Government of Bangladesh&apos;s commitment to achieve Universal Health Coverage by 2030. The activity will coordinate, collaborate, and consider engaging other stakeholders in the urban health space. The stakeholders will include the World Bank, Asian Development Bank, Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, Ministry of Local Government, Rural Development, and Cooperatives, municipalities, city corporations, urbanites, various actors within the public health system, and private healthcare providers. The activity supports goal three of the Joint Strategic Plan and ICS Mission Objective three of improving inclusive and equitable health, education, and livelihood services, especially for women, youth, and marginalized groups. The activity will advance the Indo-Pacific Strategy by working with the GoB to intensify efforts to prevent, detect, and respond to infectious diseases.FY 2024 funding will contribute to Adaptation Indirect ($1.5m), SL Indirect ($800k), Innovation ($300k) Gender Equality ($850k), GBV ($400k),GBV-CEFM ($350k), GFS ($330k), Health Workforce ($700k), Cross-Cutting HSS ($3.57m), MSN ($330k),(Macronutrients ($300k of which Vit A is $300k), PSE($500k),  Digital Technology-Indirect ($150k) and PGI (3.25m) issues.</narrative>
  </description>
